{"availability":"available","full":"dedalia-org/dedalo","name":"dedalo","description":"Dédalo: Cultural Heritage & Oral History Management System","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":51,"forks":11,"created":"2014-08-14T10:22:31Z","updated":"2026-10-15T13:14:32Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://dedalo.dev","topics":["archeology","cultural-analytics","cultural-heritage","digital-humanities","graph-database","heritage","nosql-database","ontology","openapi","oral-histories","thesaurus"],"demo":"https://demo.dedalo.dev/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:35.037Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:35.037Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:35.037Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:19.081Z","stars":49,"forks":11},{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:35.037Z","stars":51,"forks":11}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Dédalo is a knowledge management system for tangible and intangible Cultural Heritage, Natural Heritage, and Oral History and Memory. It is Free and Open Source software built on an active ontology model.","Most catalog software hard-codes its data model: a programmer decides there is a \"People\" table with a \"surname\" column, and changing that means changing code. Dédalo does the opposite. Every section (a kind of record), every field, every relation, menu, tool and button is a node in the ontology, resolved while the program runs. Reshape the catalog (add a field, turn a text box into a picker, define a new kind of record) and you do it by editing definitions, not by asking a programmer to alter tables.","The ontology can be modified at any time, subsequently changing both the data and the code. You can develop new functionalities without changing the data, and alter the metadata independently of the code and the data."],"features":["Make the data structured — user data is stored without a fixed schema, in JSONB format.","Build programming objects at runtime — components, sections, and tools are constructed from ontology definitions during execution.","Interpret and translate data — to multiple formats: RDF, JSON-LD, SQL, CSV, XML, Dublin Core, HTML, PDF, and more."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dedalia-org/dedalo/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"b25f77f22a3361536dae0daeb0e890b894c58a51f3be5cce7bd7beeeeb29c67f","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:35.205Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:35.205Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Dédalo is a knowledge management system for tangible and intangible Cultural Heritage, Natural Heritage, and Oral History and Memory. It is Free and Open Source software built on an active ontology model.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dedalia-org/dedalo/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Log in and head to the Development Area.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dedalia-org/dedalo/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Log out and log in with the admin user.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dedalia-org/dedalo/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"b25f77f22a3361536dae0daeb0e890b894c58a51f3be5cce7bd7beeeeb29c67f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dedalia-org/dedalo/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:35.206Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T13:14:32Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dedalia-org/dedalo/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:35.206Z","hash":"b25f77f22a3361536dae0daeb0e890b894c58a51f3be5cce7bd7beeeeb29c67f","originalBytes":17543,"storedBytes":17543,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["engineering","data","dalo","bun","ontology","php","system","server","every","section","diffusion","rewrite","request","client","core","docs","spec.md","test","tools","components","config","install","model","one","relations","typescript","component","heritage","parity","record","run","sa